y":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Feature already in Vim?\r\n\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n### Feature description\r\n\r\nWasn't sure whether to report as a bug (could call it a regression 🙈) or feature request (it's something I'd like to be able to), but here we are.\r\n\r\nAfter #15585 was merged, I am no longer able to redefine the signs used for diagnostics (I like setting the text so I don't have a signcolumn, having a diagnostic just causes the linenumber to change color). The signs are defined whenever the diagnostics are displayed for the first time, so overriding it is very tricky.\r\n\r\nI'm using a weird workaround for now:\r\n\r\nOverride the handler for publishDiagnostics so it:\r\n\r\n1. Calls vim.lsp.diagnostic.on_publish_diagnostics\r\n2. Checks whether there are any diagnostics in the result\r\n3. If so, redefine the signs, call vim.diagnostic.reset and call vim.lsp.diagnostic.on_publish_diagnostics again (yes, it's awful)\r\n\r\nHere is the code if anyone is interested: https://github.com/fsouza/dotfiles/blob/758eb06e94eaaf8ba3513da878615610f1b2ed2b/nvim/lua/fsouza/lsp/buf_diagnostic.lua#L42-L51\r\n\r\nI imagine some other plugins will want to override the signs too (with emojis and what not), so this is probably a legit use-case?\r\n\r\nPerhaps I'm missing something though, so please feel free to tell I'm just wrong :)","closed_by":{"login":"justinmk","id":1359421,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTk0MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk","html_url":"https://github.com/justinmk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"http